Package: xios-core
Name: Xios Desktop Core
Version: 0.1.11
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Maintainer: Max Leiter <maxwell.leiter@gmail.com>
Author: Max Leiter <maxwell.leiter@gmail.com>
Section: Desktop
Priority: optional
Depends: firmware (>= 16.5), xios-runtime (>= 0.1.4), com.max.xios (>= 0.1.7), iosc (>= 0.9.43), iosc-shell (>= 0.9.11), xios-session (>= 1.0.75)
MinimumOSVersion: 16.5.0
Description: shared base for Xios fullscreen desktop flavors
 The common presentation layer used by the fullscreen Xios desktop flavors:
 the Xios display app (Home Screen icon "X11"), iosc desktop shell, and session
 launcher on top of the shell-independent xios-runtime package. A desktop can
 be started from inside the app or with xios-session on the command line.
 .
 Install one of the flavor packages instead of this one: xios-gnome,
 xios-kde, or xios-x11. Each pulls in xios-core automatically. The native
 iPadOS flavor intentionally uses xios-runtime without this fullscreen shell.
 .
 The display app is unsigned and needs AppSync Unified (from the
 https://cydia.akemi.ai/ repo) to launch. Rootless jailbreaks only (/var/jb).
